            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "A dog treadmill is built around a dog: a running area sized to a four-legged stride, side panels to keep the dog centred, nothing at nose height at the front, a lower step-on and a stop the owner can reach from beside the machine. A human treadmill assumes a user who can see the edges, hold the rails and pull a safety key.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
