          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Some healthy adult dogs can walk slowly on one, with an owner beside the machine throughout, after a vet has agreed. It is a compromise: the belt is usually short for a trotting dog, the motor hood sits at nose height and there are no side panels. Never tether the dog, never leave it, and stop at any sign of stress.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
