            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "A dog cannot see or feel the edges of a moving belt the way a person can, and will drift when anxious or distracted. Side panels give a visual boundary, keep the dog centred and stop it stepping sideways off the belt or landing half on a foot rail. On a human treadmill, only the owner standing alongside provides that guidance.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
